    "text": "By Henry J. Fromage ,\n21 hours ago “Idda” is another name locals have for Mount Etna, meaning “she” in local dialect, reflecting the belief that the volcano is living, and is female in nature. Idda follows Ita (Tecla Insolia), a photographer who wishes to finally climb Mount Etna with her friend Sofia (Romana Maggiora Vergano) as she had promised they’d do after Ita’s mother’s death. Read full article",
